---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: "Siren: AI Communications & MCP Tooling — Kiran S Baliga", description: "Zero-install Model Context Protocol (MCP) server and dual-stack agent toolkits on npm and PyPI with deterministic idempotency guards for autonomous AI agents." }}>
	<article class="pt-2 pb-10 sm:pt-4 sm:pb-14">
		<a
			class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 font-sans text-xs text-[#797974] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200 mb-6"
			href="/#work"
		>
			&larr; Back to selected work
		</a>

		{/* Article Header */}
		<header class="mb-8">
			<span class="block font-sans text-xs text-[#797974] mb-2">
				Siren &middot; Engineering case study
			</span>

			<h1 class="font-sans text-[26px] sm:text-[28px] leading-[1.25] font-normal text-[#262625] mb-3">
				Communication rails and MCP tooling for autonomous AI agents.
			</h1>

			<p class="font-sans text-[14.5px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441] max-w-2xl mb-6">
				At Siren, I engineered the developer infrastructure enabling AI agents to communicate: shared tool schemas, TypeScript and Python agent toolkits, and a standalone Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
			</p>

			{/* Role & Context Box */}
			<div class="border-y border-[#deded8] py-4">
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-2.5">
					<div>
						<span class="block font-sans text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
							Associate Software Engineer
						</span>
						<span class="font-sans text-[12.5px] text-[#797974]">
							KeyValue Software Systems &middot; Client engagement: Siren
						</span>
					</div>
					<div class="sm:text-right">
						<span class="block font-sans text-[12.5px] text-[#797974] tabular-nums">
							Sep 2023&ndash;Feb 2026
						</span>
						<a
							class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200"
							href="https://trysiren.io"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							trysiren.io &nearr;
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="font-mono text-[11.5px] text-[#797974] leading-relaxed">
					Model Context Protocol (MCP) &middot; TypeScript &middot; Python &middot; OpenAI Functions &middot; LangChain &middot; CrewAI
				</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		{/* Context */}
		<section class="space-y-3 mb-8">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[16px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				The context
			</h2>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				Siren provides omni-channel messaging and notification infrastructure. As autonomous agent workflows (OpenAI Function Calling, LangChain, CrewAI) began executing user-facing tasks, agents needed safe, deterministic ways to trigger notifications, verify recipients, and inspect delivery status without manual API integration.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				The core architectural goal was to turn imperative REST API endpoints into clean, agent-readable semantic tool schemas with strict parameter boundaries and deterministic execution safeguards.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Zero-Install MCP Server */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8 space-y-3.5">
			<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] uppercase tracking-wider block">
				Architecture 01
			</span>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				Zero-install Model Context Protocol (MCP) server
			</h2>

			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				I built and distributed <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[#f4f3ef] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[#262625]">@trysiren/mcp</code>, a standalone server implementing Anthropic’s Model Context Protocol. Supporting both stdio and Server-Sent Events (SSE) transports, it allowed AI coding assistants (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Antigravity) to send notifications directly from developer environments.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				This eliminated ~75% of developer setup overhead: rather than installing libraries, importing HTTP clients, and managing secret rotation in application code, developers execute the server with zero installation via <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[#f4f3ef] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[#262625]">npx @trysiren/mcp</code>.
			</p>

			<div class="border-l-2 border-[#16a34a] pl-4 py-1.5 my-3">
				<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
					Making existing products AI-native doesn’t require rebuilding the backend. It requires building an intuitive, deterministic discovery and execution layer for models.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Dual-Stack SDKs & Idempotency */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8 space-y-3.5">
			<span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#797974] uppercase tracking-wider block">
				Architecture 02
			</span>

			<h2 class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625]">
				Dual-stack agent toolkits with idempotency guards
			</h2>

			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				For programmatic multi-agent swarms, I authored and published <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[#f4f3ef] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[#262625]">@trysiren/agent-toolkit</code> on npm and <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-[#f4f3ef] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[#262625]">siren-agent-toolkit</code> on PyPI. Both feature automatic conversion adapters for LangChain Tools and CrewAI Actions.
			</p>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] sm:text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[#444441]">
				Because LLM tool-calling can trigger stochastic retry loops, we embedded deterministic idempotency key derivation directly into the toolkits. Multiple identical intents from an agent resolve to the same underlying dispatch, preventing accidental notification spam.
			</p>
		</section>

		{/* Quantified Impact */}
		<section class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6 mb-8">
			<h2 class="font-sans text-[16px] font-medium text-[#262625] mb-4">
				What changed
			</h2>

			<div class="space-y-3.5">
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#16a34a] w-32 shrink-0">
						~75%
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Reduction in developer setup effort with zero-install MCP vs. manual SDK integration.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625] w-32 shrink-0">
						100+
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Peak registry downloads across npm and PyPI ecosystem distributions.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 border-b border-[#deded8] pb-3">
					<span class="font-sans text-[18px] sm:text-[20px] font-medium text-[#262625] w-32 shrink-0">
						&lt;1ms
					</span>
					<p class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#444441]">
						Serialization overhead across schema parsing and parameter validation pipelines.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Navigation Footer */}
		<div class="border-t border-[#deded8] pt-6">
			<div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-2">
				<span class="font-sans text-xs text-[#797974]">Next case study</span>
				<a
					class="font-sans text-[13.5px] text-[#262625] hover:text-accent transition-colors duration-200"
					href="/work/ultrahuman/"
				>
					Ultrahuman &mdash; clinical LLM pipelines &rarr;
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="font-sans text-[13px] text-[#797974] mt-3">
				Building agent tooling or Model Context Protocol integrations? <a class="underline hover:text-accent text-[#262625]" href="mailto:kiransbaliga@gmail.com">Let’s talk about it.</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
